    "notes": "107 lessons (1.html-107.html); index.html is a JS redirect to lesson 1 and is excluded; no duplicate or draft lessons. Numbering is fully contiguous 1-107 with no gaps and follows a coherent topical curriculum (Trigonometry 1-10, Limits 11-16, Derivatives 17-26, Integrals 27-34, Exp/Log 35-39, Functions 40-46, Polynomials/Equations 47-62, Sequences/Series 63-67, Complex 68-71, Matrices 72-75, Analytic Geometry 76-81, Plane/Solid Geometry 82-93, Probability 94-101, Statistics 102-107) — no ordering issues. SOURCE TITLES ARE ENGLISH (html lang=en; <title> = 'EN Title — Math — Mikail Sarpkaya'); the tr hreflang points to the same English URL, so there is no separate Turkish page content. 'en' holds the verbatim page title; 'tr' is a translation; slugs are concise transliterated Turkish per the strict ruleset and are unique within this track. SLUG/TOPIC OVERLAP WITH 'ales' TRACK (which already has Turkish slugs): heavy conceptual overlap but this is a deeper YKS/AYT-style course vs ALES exam-prep, so slugs were kept track-local and only partially aligned to ALES wording. Direct topic equivalents include matematik 2 (temel-trigonometrik-oranlar) ~ ales/56 'Trigonometri Temel Oranlar'; 54 (ikinci-derece-denklemler) = ales/26; 63 (aritmetik-diziler)=ales/41; 64 (geometrik-diziler)=ales/42; 79 (cember-denklemi)~ales/52 'Çember ve Daire'; 86 (dortgenler) & 88 (cevre-ve-alan)~ales polygon/area; 98 (permutasyon)=ales/43; 99 (kombinasyon)=ales/44; 94 (olasilik-temelleri)~ales/45 'Olasılık'; 50 (carpanlara-ayirma-teknikleri)~ales/30; 38/logaritmik & 36 ~ales/32 'Logaritma'; turev cluster 17-26 ~ales/61 'Türev'; integral cluster 27-34 ~ales/62 'İntegral'; limit cluster 11-16 ~ales/60 'Limit ve Süreklilik'; 40-44 functions ~ales/31. NOTE the ales track also ships duplicate slug-named html files (e.g. dogal-sayilar.html alongside 1.html); matematik currently ships only numbered files, so this migration is what introduces its slugs. CONTENT GAPS vs ales: matematik has NO number-theory/arithmetic-problem lessons (doğal/tam/rasyonel sayılar, bölünebilme, EBOB-EKOK, oran-orantı, yüzde, faiz, hız/işçi/yaş/karışım word-problems, modüler aritmetik) that ales covers; conversely ales lacks matematik's vectors (91), conics (80-81), De Moivre (71), matrices/determinants (72-75), curve sketching (25) and the statistics block (100-107). Lessons 105 & 107 are explicitly marked '(Preview)' in their titles (early/preview content, not full lessons) — flagged though not true drafts."
